# AllGo Production Engineering Rules (always_on)

## 1. Strict Code Modularity & File Size Laws
- Every file MUST have a single, well-defined responsibility.
- Keep individual source files strictly under 100 to 250 lines (never exceed 300 lines). If a file grows larger, split sub-modules into dedicated files.
- Frontend/Mobile directory structure MUST strictly follow:
  - `src/pages/` (screen-level route containers only)
  - `src/components/` (reusable, stateless or isolated UI widgets; use `AppIcon.tsx` and `src/design-system/iconAssets.ts` for all icons)
  - `src/data/` (isolated data/network modules: `apiClient.ts`, `smsAuthLoader.ts`, `liveOrderStream.ts`, `gpsLoader.ts`, `paymentGateway.ts`, `localCache.ts`)

## 2. Environment, Network & Build Constraints
- NEVER hardcode `a.lvh.me:3000`, `localhost`, or raw API keys in source code.
- Default production backend base URL is `https://allgo-api.onrender.com` (injectable via environment/compile-time variables).
- Always compile `@allgo/common` (`npm run build --workspace=@allgo/common`) BEFORE building or testing `allgo-api` or client apps.
- On local Windows Android/Flutter builds, ensure `GRADLE_USER_HOME` points to `E:\.gradle` if `C:\Users` cache write locks occur, and pass `--android-skip-build-dependency-validation` when required.
- Never commit `build/`, `.gradle/`, `node_modules/`, or raw `google-services.json` secrets to git.
